              "type": "text",
              "text": "Find the coordinates of the points where the graphs of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "y = 2x + 3",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "y = \\frac{2}{x}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " intersect.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\left(\\frac{1}{2},4\\right)$ and $(-2,-1)$.",
      "worked": "Equate the expressions for $y$, with $x\\ne0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+3&=\\frac{2}{x}\\\\2x^2+3x-2&=0\\\\(2x-1)(x+2)&=0\\\\x&=\\frac12\\text{ or }-2\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into $y=2x+3$.\n\nFor $x=\\frac12$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2\\left(\\frac12\\right)+3\\\\y&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $x=-2$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2(-2)+3\\\\y&=-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth points satisfy the original equations. The intersection points are $\\left(\\frac12,4\\right)$ and $(-2,-1)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 80
